# Source-of-truth WordPress uploads tree — 3.0 GB, backed up off-machine.
# Local-only by decision D1 in EXECUTION.md. Only the ~700 originals that
# projects actually reference get committed, into content/images/.
# sources/UPLOADS-MANIFEST.txt records a SHA-256 for every file in it.
sources/uploads/

# Web-master images live in their own repository — decision D7.
#
#   DigitalFuturesOCADU/openShow-images   ->  checked out to content/images
#
# 710 files, 227 MB. Kept out of this repository so a colleague can clone 15 MB
# and still have every project record, every document and the whole site source
# — everything except previewing photographs locally. CI checks out both, so
# Pages builds and deploys normally.
#
# Not Git LFS: an LFS checkout in Actions spends its full size against a 10 GB
# monthly bandwidth allowance on every build, which is roughly 44 builds and
# fails at the end of a busy month rather than when anyone would notice.
#
# To work with images locally:
#   git clone https://github.com/DigitalFuturesOCADU/openShow-images content/images
# or regenerate them from sources/uploads:
#   node scripts/sync-media.mjs
content/images/

# Build artifacts
node_modules/
dist/
.astro/
.cache/

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Note: the WXR export and SQL dump are deliberately NOT ignored here.
# Step 1 relocates them to sources/ and decides tracked-vs-LFS.
sources/submissions/
inbox/*.xlsx
inbox/~$*
config/console.json
submissions/*/media/
config/overrides.yaml.bak
